WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.940
Doctor Strange might be able to enter the
Mirror Dimension, Dark Dimension, and Astral

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.500
Plane, but he also successfully transcended
to a new level of existence that is just as

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.449
impressive — the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:11.449 --> 00:00:15.129
If you're not a sorcerer's apprentice yourself,
though, you might have missed some of the

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:17.480
finer details of the film's finale.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.859
But don't worry, we've got you covered.

00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:21.599
Here's the ending of Doctor Strange explained.

00:00:21.599 --> 00:00:23.710
The secret of the eye

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:27.939
Don't tell Thanos, but the Eye of Agamotto
is actually an Infinity Stone — the Time

00:00:27.939 --> 00:00:28.939
Stone to be precise.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:33.210
For those of you keeping score at home, that's
the fifth of the six Infinity Stones to appear

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.850
in a Marvel movie so far: the Mind Stone is
in Vision's forehead, the Power Stone is held

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:43.090
by the Nova Corps, the Space Stone is in Asgard's
vault, and the Reality Stone is with the Collector.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:47.480
And since Thanos needs all six to complete
his Infinity Gauntlet, that means Dr. Strange

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.690
is on a collision course with the biggest
baddie in the known universe.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.690
Pretty sweet.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.690
The broken watch

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.199
Sorry Doctor Palmer, but after the film's
first 20 minutes, it was safe to say that

00:00:56.199 --> 00:00:59.600
Stephen Strange will always be married to
his work, not you.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.019
Nevertheless, he still wears the watch she
gave him in order to remember that great gal

00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:06.370
who stuck by his side, even back when he was
acting like a total Sherlock.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:09.830
"There are other things that can give your
life meaning!"

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:12.090
"Like what like you?"

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.360
"And this is the part where you apologize."

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.460
But that's not all the watch symbolizes.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.350
The shattered face, broken in his car accident,
is a reminder of how pride goeth before a

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.060
fall, while the inscription on the back also
prompts Strange to use the time-reversing

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.900
powers of the Eye of Agamotto to defeat Dormammu.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.130
The watch may be broken, but thanks to its
many meanings, the Earth is still ticking.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.430
The Sanctum Sanctorum

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:38.640
Kaecilius and his cronies destroyed the London
Sanctum, ruining a good portion of Kamar-Taj

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.640
in the process.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.420
And while the Hong Kong Sanctum was saved
with all that time trickery, it still took

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.220
a severe beating courtesy of Dormammu's henchmen.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:49.840
So at the end of the movie, it appears that
Doctor Strange has decided to abandon the

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.980
Ancient One's tradition of living in Tibet
and instead has made New York his full time

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.090
headquarters — just like in the comics.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.070
He probably just wanted better broadband.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.210
"Uh what's this, my mantra?"

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.430
"The wifi password.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.020
We're not savages."

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.690
Succeeding the Sorcerer Supreme

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:13.010
With the Ancient One gone, the world heavyweight
title of Sorcerer Supreme has basically been

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.400
passed down to the Doctor's broken hands.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.430
And whether or not it's official, he's definitely
earned it: he stopped Kaecilius, he came to

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:24.040
a stalemate with Dormammu, he fixed the Hong
Kong Sanctum, he was chosen by the Cloak of

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.021
Levitation, and he saved the planet.

00:02:26.021 --> 00:02:30.440
He still maintains vigilance over Kamar-Taj
and the New York Sanctum.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:34.239
And according to the mid-credits scene, he's
already fulfilling his duties by safeguarding

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:36.030
Earth from threats like Loki.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.230
Thanks, Doc!

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.230
Baron Mordo

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:42.489
So why did Baron Mordo turn his back on Dr.
Strange at the end, and then turn into a straight

00:02:42.489 --> 00:02:44.310
up villain in the post-credits scene?

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.909
Because it was fated — not by a magic prophecy,
but by the comics.

00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:51.329
Just like in the movie, comic book Mordo was
the Ancient One's apprentice.

00:02:51.329 --> 00:02:54.650
But he eventually went bad, and became Doctor
Strange's archenemy.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.800
Based on the post-credits scene, it seems
like movie Mordo is going down the same path,

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.150
meaning we expect to see a lot more of him
in the sequel — as a bad guy.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.360
"This wasn't cleverness, it was suicide!"

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.360
Thanks for watching!

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.660
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel and watch more videos like

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:11.689
the one you just saw.

00:03:11.689 --> 00:03:14.530
And don't forget to check out all this cool
stuff we know you'll love, too!

